<img width="350" height="525" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-350x525.jpg" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="CAVA&#039;s Cucumber mint lime drink in a glass garnished with a sprig of mint." style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-350x525.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-400x600.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-150x225.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-735x1103.jpg 735w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" />
<div class="wp-block-group is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p>As I set out to recreate CAVA&rsquo;s cucumber mint lime drink, I started with a base of lime juice, almost like making a classic limeade. At first, I blended cucumber juice, lime juice, and a bit of simple syrup. It was good, but honestly, it just tasted like limeade. It was nothing memorable.</p>



<p>Then I came across a tip that suggested enhancing limeade with lime zest and a splash of lemon juice. That tip was golden. Those two small additions completely transformed my simple drink into something bright, layered, and refreshing, and more importantly, just like the version I love at CAVA.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Cucumber-mint-drink.jpg" alt="CAVA copycat mint lime cucumber drink in glasses garnished with mint lime, and cucumber slices." class="wp-image-82656" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Cucumber-mint-drink.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Cucumber-mint-drink-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Cucumber-mint-drink-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Cucumber-mint-drink-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Cucumber-mint-drink-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Cucumber-mint-drink.jpg"></figure>



<p>This homemade cucumber mint lime juice drink recipe has that exact light, crisp, and not overly sweet flavor. It&rsquo;s also incredibly easy to customize, can be served non-alcoholic or as a cocktail, and is also make-ahead friendly, making it a total crowd-pleaser for any warm day. Not to mention, making your own is way more cost-effective than buying at the store.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-cava-cucumber-mint-lime-ingredients">Cava Cucumber Mint Lime Ingredients</h2>



<p>To make this copycat CAVA cucumber mint limeade, you only need a few simple, fresh ingredients you probably already have in your fridge/pantry. You&rsquo;ll find the full list in the recipe card below, but here are a few helpful notes from my testing:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-ingredients-1200x800.jpg" alt="Ingredients for the recipe from the top view with text on the image." class="wp-image-82657" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-ingredients.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-ingredients-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-ingredients-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-ingredients-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-ingredients-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CAVA-cucumber-mint-lime-ingredients.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>For the Mint Simple Syrup</strong></p>



<p><strong>Sweetener:</strong> Traditionally, simple syrup uses equal parts sugar and water. I like to use honey (or agave syrup) instead, inspired by my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/honey-simple-syrup/">Honey Simple Syrup recipe</a>, to keep the drink naturally sweetened. Both options work beautifully.</p>



<p><strong>Mint: </strong>Any fresh mint you grow or can find in your local supermarket will do. Peppermint or spearmint are both great choices.</p>



<p><strong>For the Drink</strong></p>



<p><strong>Cucumbers:</strong> I prefer Persian cucumbers for their crisp, sweet taste, but English cucumbers are a great substitute. Peeling is optional, but if you keep the skin on, give it a taste first to make sure it&rsquo;s not bitter, since older cucumber skins can sometimes be tough and a bit bitter.</p>



<p><strong>Lime and Lemon Juice &amp; Zest:</strong> Freshly squeezed juice is best for a bright, clean taste. Bottled juice works in a pinch, but if you can, squeeze your own. When I was testing this recipe, I noticed that using only the juice didn&rsquo;t quite capture the citrusy kick that makes CAVA&rsquo;s version so refreshing. </p>



<p>That&rsquo;s when I decided to add the zest of both lime and lemon. It turned out to be the missing piece, bringing the drink much closer to the one I first enjoyed at CAVA.</p>



<p><strong>Ice:</strong> Cubed or crushed ice keeps the drink cold and refreshing.</p>



<p><strong>For the Garnishes</strong></p>



<p>This is where you can have some fun. Add cucumber slices, sliced lime, or fresh mint sprigs for a pretty, restaurant-style touch.</p>
</div>



